              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"ki\"]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the k- question family — ki, ke, kôbe, kōthāy, kēmon",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the k- question family — *ki, ke, kôbe, kōthāy, kēmon*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What root do Bengali's question-words share, and its English family? (The interrogative k-, PIE kʷo-; the wh- words.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "BN-C02-tumi-apni",
      "sequence": 120,
      "title": "তুমি / আপনি (tumi / āpni) — \"you,\" three ways",
      "headword": "তুমি / আপনি",
      "romanization": "",
      "gloss": "you (familiar / respectful; also তুই intimate)",
      "script": "bengali",
      "modality": "sight",
      "derivedModality": "sight",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "script-block"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:ecf9c947f3fe4048",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "sight",
        "needs": [
          "your eyes, for letter shapes on the page"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "The letters in this word"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your eyes, so it is not fully a driving lesson. You will want your eyes, for letter shapes on the page. You can listen to everything else now — leave the section called The letters in this word until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "To ask a name you need \"you\" — and Bengali grades it three ways."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "The letters in this word",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তুমি (tumi): তু (tu) + মি (mi). আপনি (āpni): আ + প."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "নি."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তুমি (tumi, familiar \"you\") from Sanskrit tvam, from PIE tū — the same root as English archaic thou, Latin tū, French tu. Bengali grades respect in three levels:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তুই (tui) — intimate: close friends, children, family."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তুমি (tumi) — familiar: friends, juniors, warmth."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আপনি (āpni) — respectful: elders, strangers, formality."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "(This is like Hindi's tū / tum / āp, and finer than the two-way split of the Romance tracks.) For a first meeting, use আপনি."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the three — tui (intimate) / tumi (familiar) / āpni (respectful)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the three — *tui* (intimate) / *tumi* (familiar) / *āpni* (respectful)]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the English cousin of tumi (thou)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the English cousin of *tumi* (**thou**)]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "which you use on first meeting (āpni)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: which you use on first meeting (*āpni*)]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
